nghai's  fudan university claims that with the  currently low vaccination rate among  elderly people  the lifting of the zero cove policy  could lead to over 1.5 million deaths  china could have pushed for a more  aggressive vaccination campaign before  the omicron variant appeared  missing that window has resulted in the  struggle it's facing today  that wasn't really planning for the  future and wasn't really planning for  the contingency of a more transmissible  variant as we've seen on top of that  there's a question of vaccine efficacy  research has shown that the chinese-made  inactivated virus vaccines are less  effective against infections with  omicron than mrna vaccines like for  example the visor beyond that vaccine  but china still hasn't approved the use  of foreign-made vaccines for its  population  instead it is betting on home-grown mlna  vaccines which are still undergoing  clinical trials  and that seems to be driven purely by by  political  decisions you know political motives to  not want to be seen to be reliant on  international support international  science and technology but to be able to  develop their own vaccines and use them  this possibility of high death rates and  infections if china drops its zero  co-feed approach is just too risky for  the ruling communist party a lot of how  people see 20  c covid 2020 2021  is in comparison with the west you know  so  in countries like the united states and  western european countries coveted rates  were very high death rates were very  high  people had waves of lockdown and  a lot of political disturbances and you  know it just felt like chaos in the west  whereas china was relatively peaceful  and have very low death rates  professor nancy chen is currently based  in the u.s  she has been observing and writing about  china's covet  think that's what the strategy  want to avoid and they just don't know  how i mean they can't avoid it  completely they have to find they're  trying to find the path  of minimal political cost  and the political cost of abandoning the  zero kofi strategy currently seems to be  too high  it has become president xi's signature  policy  he is expected to announce his intention  for landmark third term at china's 20th  party congress coming up in september  so it would be bad timing for a game  bowl on a new way to handle the pandemic  they  think that they have demonstrated the  superiority of the system in containing  the virus  and therefore they would like they would  like to continue with that and they  think they can continue with that  but the costs of continuing with the  policy are growing  the stringent kofi strategy is taking  its toll not only on people's daily  lives but also on china's economy  and that too will tarnish the ruling  party's popularity  is there a way then for china to both  transition out of its zero kovi strategy  and save the party's image  i believe that it should be possible for  them to find  a face-saving way to message this right  it's all about the messaging to say look  there's going to be some risks but if we  don't open up there are other types of  risks and others constantly have to pay  the difficulty is that the longer they  go on as they are now  the harder it will be for them to do  that messaging effectively because the  longer they go on like they do now the  more unhappy people are and the less  people trust the government  and this all leaves xi jinping and the  communist party in a particularly tricky  situation they do just seem to think  that they can keep testing and  containing their way out of this  however long term  it doesn't look very it doesn't look  very sustainable there is going to be a  political hit no matter what they can't  escape it  you

